---
// Verbatim Authentic Content & Media from Khao Sok Riverside Cottages
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Fungal in the Jungle – the Hidden Mushrooms of Khao Sok"
  description="An introduction to the mushrooms of Khao Sok buy Róisín. Discover the the hidden world of mushrooms with photos and video."
  heroImage="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/stereum_ostrea-2.jpg"
  heroTitle="Fungal in the Jungle – the Hidden Mushrooms of Khao Sok"
  heroSubtitle="Handcrafted Wooden Lodging Beside the Sok River"
  breadcrumbs={[{"label": "Fungal In The Jungle The Hid...", "href": "/fungal-in-the-jungle-the-hidden-mushrooms-of-khao-sok/"}]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="bg-[#faf8f5]/95 border border-[#12281b]/10 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md">
      
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#12281b]/10 pb-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-[#163824]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold">
          <span class="text-[#7a5813]">KSR</span>
          <span class="text-[#12281b]/20">/</span>
          <span>FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-[#7a5813] font-bold">KHAO SOK · THAILAND</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#223e2c] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">

        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          When people think of Khao Sok, they usually picture the green jungle, tropical birds and stomping elephants. But scattered across the forest floor is a forgotten kingdom; the hidden world of wild mushrooms. The mushrooms of Khao Sok are often overlooked, but they are a vital part of forest ecosystems. I recently ventured deep into one of the world's oldest forests to search for these hidden gems. I couldn’t believe how much I uncovered. Let’s dive into the world of the mushrooms and explore what we found.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Finding the Fungi</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Once we hit the trail, I focused all my attention on finding mushrooms. Scanning side to side, I searched the verges of the track and on fallen logs. Fungi are everywhere, but they can be tricky to find! Mushrooms have a reputation of being elusive. That is because they are known to only fruit once or twice a year, meaning you must be really lucky to find them. Once a mushroom does fruit, it usually only lasts for a couple of days, before disappearing back into the soil.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/stereum_ostrea-2.jpg"
            alt="Stereum Ostrfea"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Stereum Ostrfea</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>Stereum ostrea</strong>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Ganoderma sp</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Some mushrooms, however, stick around for a lot longer. This humongous mushroom is a species of <em>Ganoderma</em> and has taken many years to grow to this size. Large bracket mushrooms like these ones, grow slowly from the trunks of trees.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These mushrooms release their spores from small pores on its underside. They are similar to the seeds of a plant and allow the mushroom to spread and reproduce throughout the Jungle. Billions of spores can be seen wafting like smoke from beneath this mushroom.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This mushroom will likely be here for many years to come and is located right in the middle of the <a href="/riverside-cottages-nature-trail/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">nature trail</a> at Khao Sok Riverside cottages! Drop by to have a look at this giant mushroom during your stay.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/ganoderma-e.jpg"
            alt="Ganoderma mushroom of Khao Sok"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Ganoderma mushroom of Khao Sok</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/ganoderma-2e.jpg.jpg"
            alt="Mushrooms of Khao Sok - Ganoderma"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Mushrooms of Khao Sok - Ganoderma</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>How Do the Mushrooms of Khao Sok help the Jungle?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          After a while my eyes adjust to finding fungi. Eyes opened, I notice the abundant mushrooms all around me. How different they are to everything else in the Jungle.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          You may be surprised to learn that mushrooms are not plants, but part of their own kingdom; the kingdom of Fungi!
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Mushrooms, like us, rely on sugar to obtain their energy.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>This sets them apart from their plant neighbours, who use the sun as their source of fuel.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>They get this sugar from their environment in many clever ways.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Some like to recycle, by breaking down wood, leaf litter and other organic material to get energy.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Others get their sugar from trees, through intricate symbiotic relationships.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          In all cases, mushrooms play an important ecological role in forest ecosystems. They help forests thrive, either by removing waste or supporting the growth of jungle plants.
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Cookeina speciosa</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Against the backdrop of leafy greens, there is one mushroom that is easy to spot. <em>Cookinea </em>is a striking orange and red colour. This mushroom, with its white stem and red cup, looks exactly like its common name, Champagne Glass mushroom!
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          These quirky mushrooms are found in abundance growing on decomposing logs in the Khao Sok jungle. Champagne glass mushrooms do the important job of breaking down logs and branches, returning nutrients back to the soil. They are a real treat to find and add a splash of colour to the forest floor.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cookeina-speciosa-2-e.jpg"
            alt="Cookeina speciosa"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Cookeina speciosa</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Cookeina-speciosa-e.jpg"
            alt="Cookeina speciosa"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Cookeina speciosa</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Mushrooms of Khao Sok – a Fungi Feast</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          I stop for a break along the banks of the Sok River to dig into some mid day snacks. Sitting in stillness allows me to observe the movement of the forest floor. Small mushrooms suddenly feel tall as I watch insects ascend their long stems to get to the juicy top. They are also pausing for a midday meal.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Mushrooms have another way of supporting life in the jungle:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>They provide food for many, from small critters to large animals.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Ants, termites, beetles and bugs all consume fungi daily.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>They also make great insect nests, where larvae are safe and cozy while they grow.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Small jungle animals like squirrels, frogs and birds, love to have a munch too.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Even monkeys have been caught sneaking a bite.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Schizophyllum commune</span>
        </h3>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Schizophyllum-commune.jpg"
            alt="Schizophyllum commune"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Schizophyllum commune</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This little bug is enjoying a delicious meal of Splitgill mushrooms. Splitgill mushrooms are very common across Thailand and are well known for their delicious taste. Look out for their unique gill structure, which splits into many folds near the edge!
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          An example of the gills of <em>Schizophyllum commune</em> – you can see how they split into many gills near the edges.
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Schizophyllum-commune-gills.jpg"
            alt="Schizophyllum commune gills"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Schizophyllum commune gills</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Mushrooms love the Rain</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Pack your wellies and zip up your raincoats because mushrooms thrive during the <a href="/thailand-rainy-season-is-it-a-good-time-to-visit-khao-sok/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">rainy season</a>! It is a time when fewer tourists visit Khao Sok and these shy organisms appear.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Mushrooms love the rain because they are more than 90% water.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Most of the year, fungi exist solely underground, spreading through the forest in a form known as mycelium.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>This mycelium, similar to the roots of a tree, forms vast networks of threads underneath the soil.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>When the rains begin to pour, the mycelium threads fill with water.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>This water pressure leads to the formation of our familiar above ground mushrooms.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/slide-2mycelium-g-standard-v2-4x.jpeg"
            alt="mycelium"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">mycelium</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <strong>An example of mycelium, seen covering a piece of bark</strong>
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Marasmius siccus</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          After rain, mushrooms are never far away. Some mushrooms even like to dress the part; like this one, resembling a tiny umbrella. This is the orange pinwheel mushroom, a fungus so small it is easy to miss.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>This mini mushroom grows from dead leaves and twigs.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>It has a wispy black stem and a frilly orange cap.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marasmius-siccus.jpg"
            alt="Mushrooms of Khao Sok - Marasmius siccus"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Mushrooms of Khao Sok - Marasmius siccus</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marasmius-siccus-2.jpg"
            alt="Marasmius siccus"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Marasmius siccus</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Back at the start of the trail, I bid farewell to our guide and all the Khao Sok mushrooms we saw along the way. The forest of Khao Sok did not disappoint, displaying fungi of all shapes and sizes. It may not be first on your list, but definitely consider having a look for fungi on your next trip to Khao Sok <a href="/khao-sok-national-park/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">national park</a>. You may be surprised at what you can find!
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <em>Thanks to our volunteer Róisín for this blog introducing the hidden mushrooms of Khao Sok. Please check out her amazing insights at </em><a href="http://mycologicalmemories.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors"><em>mycologicalmemories.com</em></a><em> and on Instagram @mycological_memories</em>
        </p>
        <figure class="my-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-[#12281b]/10 bg-white/50">
          <img
            src="/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/roisin-2.jpg"
            alt="Roisin Mycologist"
            class="w-full h-52 sm:h-72 md:h-80 object-cover object-center"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
           width="1200" height="800" />
          <figcaption class="p-3.5 text-xs text-[#255038] font-serif italic border-t border-[#12281b]/10 bg-[#f4efeb]/60">Roisin Mycologist</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>A Guide to Khao Sok Fungi</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park in southern Thailand has one of the oldest rainforests in the world with an abundance of plant species. Its hot, humid, and rainy climate makes it an excellent habitat for fungi. While there hasn’t been a single comprehensive list published, visitors and researchers have reported a wide variety of mushrooms and other fungi in Khao Sok national park.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Here are some types you are likely to encounter:
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Common Types of Fungi in Khao Sok</span>
        </h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Bracket and Shelf Fungi (Polypores)Found on fallen logs and dead trees.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Includes species like Ganoderma (related to reishi mushrooms) and Trametes versicolor (turkey tail).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Bioluminescent FungiSome glow-in-the-dark mushrooms are found in Thai rainforests, such as Mycena species.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>These are often seen on decaying wood at night.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Coral FungiBrightly colored, branching fungi that look like underwater coral.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span>Common in the organic matter in moist forest floors.</span>
          </li>
